I am moving the main effort away from the collector’s missing escape saddle. Even granting complete chemical survival, the retained collector does not yet offer a sufficiently strong manufacturing operation to justify that campaign.The stronger construction developed here is post-assembly control of a crystal’s local isotope arrangement, using a returning silicon atom to exchange carbon atoms in graphene. It now has an exact controllability result: under direct Si–C exchange, two adjacent hexagons suffice to rearrange all nine host-carbon positions while returning silicon to its starting site. For two carbon isotopes, every arrangement with the same isotope count is reachable.That is a conditional construction, not an established isotope-writing process. The decisive chemical question has become sharper: does an observed silicon move transfer the intended carbon atom—or sometimes replace it through an unresolved adatom excursion? Published trajectories support both direct exchange and more complicated histories. This distinction changes the useful operation even when the final image looks correct.Why the collector no longer receives the main effortIn the retained same-host calculation, ordinary charge-equilibrated annealing gave a best target occupancy of approximately 0.121 at 36 hours. The finite collector layer raised the loss-free best occupancy to approximately 0.201 at 470 hours. These are results for the specified geometry and preparation, not universal collection limits.The more aggressive layer constructions remain potentially stronger, but require additional control of the dopant profile, electrostatics and defect chemistry. A favourable escape saddle would establish that a particular collection trajectory survives. It would not itself provide lateral placement, a selected atomic destination, controlled occupancy, or a way to verify the desired final defect.Actual processing alternatives set a demanding standard. Charge-assisted defect formation has been demonstrated in diamond, and laser processing with fluorescence feedback has produced individual NV centres at selected locations. Those results concern different hosts and, principally, creation rather than relocation; they do not establish a numerical efficiency bound for the SiC collector. They do demonstrate integrated operations in which processing, destination and useful output are connected. www.nature.com+1I therefore retain the collector as a coupled transport-and-chemistry result, including:the distinction between increased storage and increased transition-path conductance;the trajectory-weighted exposure calculation;the finite-layer collection results;the distinction between reaction formation energies and escape rates.The allocation decision does not require either a universal collection ceiling or a rapid-destruction claim. Its favourable outcome is presently too limited to make the missing saddle the most valuable next scientific input.The selected operation: rewrite mass arrangement while restoring elemental structureThe target is a local operation on an existing covalent material:Rearrange selected carbon isotopes, preserve their count, and return the silicon mediator and the required surrounding structure to their initial positions.This changes a variable that ordinary elemental imaging largely hides: the spatial arrangement of nuclear masses.The physical contact is established. Electron irradiation of a carbon neighbour can drive a Si–C exchange in graphene, with the carbon trajectory redirected by the silicon–carbon interaction. Directed silicon motion, repeated back-and-forth exchanges and closed hexagon routes have already been demonstrated. Consequently, neither silicon positioning nor a closed hexagon loop is a new invention claim here. arxiv.org+1The proposed extension is to use those operations to control the host arrangement left behind after the mediator returns.The destination is an existing lattice site. Capture is supplied by the same bond rearrangement that produces motion. This avoids assigning an independent attractive destination to a mobile species. It also exposes a stringent requirement: the completed reaction must implement the intended host-atom mapping, not merely move silicon to the next visible site.The initial scientific use would be controlled changes to a local isotope environment in the same covalent sheet. Isotope-engineered graphene already shows substantial changes in thermal behaviour when its isotope composition is changed during growth. The remaining opportunity is finer control of spatial arrangement at fixed composition and elemental structure. That distinction could support direct tests of local vibrational response and isotope correlations; it does not yet establish a thermal device or a bulk-manufacturing advantage. arxiv.orgAn exact writing operation, and its extension beyond three sitesConsider adjacent hexagons sharing the edge s−as-as−a, with silicon initially at sss:A:s→a→b→c→d→e→s,A:\quad s\to a\to b\to c\to d\to e\to s ,A:s→a→b→c→d→e→s,B:s→a→f→g→h→i→s.B:\quad s\to a\to f\to g\to h\to i\to s .B:s→a→f→g→h→i→s.Each arrow is one nearest-neighbour Si–C exchange. Run, in order,A,B,A−1,B−1.A,\quad B,\quad A^{-1},\quad B^{-1}.A,B,A−1,B−1.This requires 24 exchanges. Tracking distinct carbon labels gives:Original carbon siteFinal siteaaaffffffbbbbbbaaaEvery other host siteIts original siteSilicon returns to sss.Thus the operation cycles three selected host atoms while restoring everything else in this finite construction. If two of those atoms have the same isotope, it can move the differing isotope between chosen sites without changing the isotope identity of the buffer pair.This is an exact result of the exchange model. It does not assume a force that sorts isotopes, an isotope-selective capture site, or an additional actuator.The nine-site controllability resultThe two hexagon operations generate more than this one three-cycle.Each closed hexagon route is a five-cycle of its host carbons. Both are even permutations. Their commutator supplies a three-cycle involving sites from both hexagons. Conjugating that three-cycle by repeated hexagon routes supplies further three-cycles.The reachability argument can be completed as follows:One set of conjugates generates all even permutations on six host sites: the five carbons of one hexagon together with a carbon from the other.Conjugating this six-site action by the other hexagon route produces overlapping six-site actions.Their overlaps contain enough common sites to extend the action to all nine host sites.All generators are even, so the generated group is exactly the alternating group on nine objects, A9A_9A9​. I also enumerated the finite permutation space independently: it contains 181,440 reachable permutations, equal to 9!/29!/29!/2.For two isotope species, the apparent parity restriction disappears at the level of mass patterns. If a permutation carrying one mass pattern into another is odd, exchanging two identical-isotope labels changes its parity without changing the physical mass pattern. Therefore:Every nine-site isotope arrangement with a fixed isotope count is reachable.\boxed{\text{Every nine-site isotope arrangement with a fixed isotope count is reachable.}}Every nine-site isotope arrangement with a fixed isotope count is reachable.​For example, a cell containing four heavy and five light carbons has all(94)=126\binom{9}{4}=126(49​)=126mass arrangements accessible while returning silicon.This is a useful local controllability result, not a claim of new permutation mathematics. Its materials content is the identification of a demonstrated molecular exchange actuator that could implement the generators.Two limitations that the construction itself provesFirst, an isolated transposition of two distinguishable host atoms is unavailable in the restricted model when silicon returns. The honeycomb lattice is bipartite, so a returning silicon walk has an even number of exchanges. Its host permutation must therefore be even. The three-cycle respects this constraint.Second, blind permutation does not manufacture order from an independent random isotope mixture. If the initial isotope field is independent and identically distributed, applying a fixed permutation leaves its distribution unchanged. Completing the same prescribed route more slowly on some isotope arrangements does not change that fact in the loss-free, unconditional ensemble.Useful writing therefore needs either a known initial isotope pattern or information-dependent control. Selecting only unusually fast or surviving runs can bias the accepted ensemble, but that selection is an additional operation with its own exposure and yield costs.Reading the isotope is part of the manufacturing problemThe published graphene isotope-imaging result does not provide an unrestricted single-site identity map. Its effective sampling region contains roughly four carbon atoms, and the authors identify further improvements needed for more confident monatomic identification. I have therefore not treated that work as a free nine-site isotope readout. arxiv.org+1I instead examined a reversible kinetic read.Suppose the same carbon atom is exchanged back and forth with silicon, and the pair is returned before a read decision is accepted. If the calibrated exchange rates for the two isotopes are λ12\lambda_{12}λ12​ and λ13\lambda_{13}λ13​, observing nnn exchanges during total exposure TTT gives, in the simple exponential model,log⁡L12L13=nlog⁡λ12λ13−(λ12−λ13)T.\log\frac{\mathcal L_{12}}{\mathcal L_{13}}
